"The reeve's son Dunstan Morrow rides with the crew, and hates it."
"Osric Fenn pays the crew a share and tells them which carts carry coin."
"Voss means to take Fenwatch before the first frost, some weeks off, for its stores and crystals."
"Dunstan would turn on Voss to save Fenwatch, if someone gave him the chance."
"Of Voss's eleven, two live: the cairn lookouts Dunstan Morrow and Ulrik Hask, an Iron March man."
"Since Voss fell, Ulrik means to toll the road alone; Dunstan wants out and hides at the hollow oak."
